# Tech Stack

## Next.js 15 App Router
- Server Components by default — add `"use client"` only when interactivity is needed
- `params` and `searchParams` are Promises in Next.js 15 — always `await params` in dynamic routes
- Never `fetch()` to own API routes for mutations — use Server Actions
- Cache invalidation: `revalidatePath(path)` after mutations · `unstable_cache` for expensive reads
- New pages need `export const metadata: Metadata = { title: "... | WeMaAd Invoice" }`
- Wrap async data fetching in `<Suspense>` with a `loading.tsx` sibling

## React 19
- No `forwardRef` needed — refs are regular props
- This codebase uses React Hook Form + `toFormData`, not `useActionState`

## shadcn/ui
- Install components: `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <component-name>`
- Never edit files in `components/ui/` — they are generated; customize via Tailwind class props
- Icons: `lucide-react` — match icon style of existing components

## Prisma 6
- After any schema change: `pnpm prisma migrate dev --name <description>` (client auto-regenerates)
- No soft deletes — hard delete with `onDelete: Cascade` on all user-scoped relations
- New models need `@@index([userId])` and `@@index` on any field used in `where` filters

## NextAuth v5 (beta)
- Email magic-link only — no OAuth providers, no passwords in this project
- `auth()` → Server Components and API route handlers
- `requireUser()` / `requireAdmin()` → dashboard pages and Server Actions (redirect on failure)

## Vitest
- Environment: node · `@/*` alias resolves to project root
- Test files: `app/actions/__tests__/<domain>.test.ts`
- Run: `pnpm test` · watch: `pnpm test:watch`
- Standard mock: `vi.mock("@/lib/db", () => ({ default: { model: { fn: vi.fn() } } }))`
